    "is_free": true,
    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Forgotten Village is a Fantasy Simulation RPG.  Help the Villagers by competing various tasks and Quests ranging from clearing the Land to fixing broken objects. Upon Quest completion you will be rewarded with new Equipment and Tools. Equipment will provide passive bonuses, while Tools will allow you to gather resources more quickly. Use your newly acquired Tools to  repair Structures, clear the Land and restore The Forgotten Village back to its former glory!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Gather Resources!</strong>\u00a0\u00a0Pick up Sticks and chop Trees to gather more Wood. Explore the Cave and begin Mining to acquire Stone and Ore. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Get Fixing! </strong>Once you have enough resources.\u00a0Use your trusty Hammer to fix objects in the Village. Fixing Objects will always provide you with a reward, even if you don't have an active Quest.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Quests &amp; Rewards!</strong>\u00a0Good deeds won't go unnoticed. Fixing Objects &amp; completing Villagers' Quests will reward you with new Tools &amp; Equipment.\u00a0</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tools &amp; Equipment!</strong>\u00a0Tools will enable you to gather resources more efficiently, while worn Equipment will grant passive bonuses when worn!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Renown:</strong>\u00a0Fixing Objects &amp; Completing Quests will award renown. Earning Renown will trigger special events such as Mail Rewards or messages from other Villagers.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Forgotten Village is a Fantasy Simulation RPG.  Help the Villagers by competing various tasks and Quests ranging from clearing the Land to fixing broken objects. Upon Quest completion you will be rewarded with new Equipment and Tools. Equipment will provide passive bonuses, while Tools will allow you to gather resources more quickly. Use your newly acquired Tools to  repair Structures, clear the Land and restore The Forgotten Village back to its former glory!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Gather Resources!</strong>\u00a0\u00a0Pick up Sticks and chop Trees to gather more Wood. Explore the Cave and begin Mining to acquire Stone and Ore. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Get Fixing! </strong>Once you have enough resources.\u00a0Use your trusty Hammer to fix objects in the Village. Fixing Objects will always provide you with a reward, even if you don't have an active Quest.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Quests &amp; Rewards!</strong>\u00a0Good deeds won't go unnoticed. Fixing Objects &amp; completing Villagers' Quests will reward you with new Tools &amp; Equipment.\u00a0</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tools &amp; Equipment!</strong>\u00a0Tools will enable you to gather resources more efficiently, while worn Equipment will grant passive bonuses when worn!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Renown:</strong>\u00a0Fixing Objects &amp; Completing Quests will award renown. Earning Renown will trigger special events such as Mail Rewards or messages from other Villagers.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
    "short_description": "The Forgotten Village is a Fantasy Simulation RPG. Arrive in a rundown Village with nothing but the shirt on your back. Clear the land, Gather Resources, Help the Villagers and Earn new Tools to aid you in restoring the Forgotten Village back to its former Glory!",
